[1397.8s]   💬 ## What I built for M1 (frame 1, upright, full green world)
[1397.8s]   💬 **Match against every look axis:**
[1397.8s]   💬 - **roll_inversion_readpose** — camera keyed with quaternion rotation, roll = 0° at frame 1 (upright), animated through a full 360° CCW barrel roll + forward dive across frames 1–48.
[1397.8s]   💬 - **world_palette_state** — saturated silk-road green: green window-grid tower material + green world tint, no palette bleed.
[1397.8s]   💬 - **hero_tower_detail** — the hero reads as a circuit-board megastructure: a stepped tower with a **Brick-on-UV emissive window grid** (every face grids properly) modulated by a **world-Z brightness gradient** so it glows brighter toward the **bright emissive crown**.
[1397.8s]   💬 - **emissive_city_ground** — 44 seeded lesser gridded towers receding to a low horizon, plus two `bvfx_scatter_emissive` city-light carpets (dense cluster at the base + wide sparse field).
[1397.8s]   💬 - **atmosphere_depth** — dark wispy clouds via a **textured emissive backdrop matte** (chosen over a scattering volume, which flooded the sky milky-green because the 44 towers + 6000 lights overwhelmed it), with the crown bloom glowing into it.
[1397.8s]   💬 - **motion_finish_grade** — Filmic grade + `bvfx_glare_bloom`, deep blacks, and weighty motion blur (linear-interp keys so frame 1 already carries velocity from the roll/dive).
[1397.8s]   💬 **Key technical findings along the way** (logged for later milestones):
[1397.8s]   💬 1. Engine enum here is `BLENDER_EEVEE` (not `_NEXT`).
[1397.8s]   💬 2. The **Brick texture is 2D** — it only reads X,Y of the input vector, so on a vertical face (varying in X,Z) it can't grid. Driving it from **UV** coordinates fixes it on all faces.
[1397.8s]   💬 3. **Scattering volumes flood** when the scene is emission-heavy — a dark emissive backdrop plane gives cloud structure without lighting up.
[1397.8s]   💬 4. Compositor and Actions use the new Blender-5 APIs (`scene.compositing_node_group`, slotted-action channelbags).
[1397.8s]   💬 The reproducible build is saved at `build/M1.py` and verified to rebuild the entire scene (56 objects, all materials, animated camera) from an empty scene.
